  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public Administration Reform Monitoring PARM - PARM-Sida</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Public Administration Reform Monitoring PARM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall objective of the Public Administration Reform Monitoring (PARM) project is to capture the more immediate and concrete impact of the implementation of PAR as well as the progress in the implementation of the major objectives of the Government&#x2019;s institutional and public administration reform agenda.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Transparency International i Bosnien och Hercegovina (TI BIH), tillsammans med Center for Investigative Journalism (CIN), ans&#xf6;kte 2013 till Sida om finansiering p&#xe5; 6 miljoner kronor f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra projektet Public Administration Reform Monitoring (PARM) under en tre&#xe5;rsperiod. Danmark som tillsammans (och via) Sverige medfinansierar en fond f&#xf6;r public administration reform (PARCO-fund) visade intresse att st&#xf6;dja &#xe4;ven denna insats. Det specifika m&#xe5;let med denna insats &#xe4;r att s&#xe4;tta st&#xf6;rre tryck p&#xe5; genomf&#xf6;randet av reformer inom den offentliga sektorn genom informations- och lobbyinginsatser fr&#xe5;n det civila samh&#xe4;llet.
Danmark har d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r bidragit med ytterligare 1,5 miljoner danska kronor (cirka 1,75 mSEK) f&#xf6;r projektgenomf&#xf6;randet vilket resulterade i projektperioden kan f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngas ytterligare ett &#xe5;r med en ut&#xf6;kad budget. TI/CIN har d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r justerat den ursprungliga arbetsplanen och budgeten med h&#xe4;nsyn till det nya totalbeloppet p&#xe5; 7,75 MSEK f&#xf6;r fyra &#xe5;r. Projektet kommer att genomf&#xf6;ras under perioden 2014-2018 .</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transparency International in Bosnia and Herzegovina (TI BIH ), together with the Center for Investigative Journalism (CIN) , applied in 2013 to Sida for funding of 6 million SEK to implement the project Public Administration Reform Monitoring (PARM) over a three year period. Denmark, which together (and through) Sweden is co-financing a fund for the public administration reform (PARCO fund), showed interest to support even this effort. The specific objective of this contribution is to put more pressure on the implementation of reforms in the public sector through information and lobbying efforts by civil society.
Denmark decided to contribute an additional 1.5 million Danish kroner ( approximately 1.75 mSEK ) for project implementation which resulted in the project period to be extended for an additional year with an additional budget . TI/CIN has therefore adjusted the original work plan and budget to match the new total of 7.75 million for four years. The project will be implemented over the period 2014-2018 .</narrative>
  </description>
